1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,827
You can be wrong most of the time, and still make money. Here's how.

2
00:00:05,850 --> 00:00:10,694
Compare what you risk with what you aim to make. Red is the risk, green is the target.

3
00:00:11,063 --> 00:00:14,870
Risking one to make one is very different from risking one to make three.

4
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:21,066
At one to three, you can be wrong three times out of four, and still roughly break even.

5
00:00:21,414 --> 00:00:25,199
But the target has to be realistic, like the next resistance level.

6
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:28,416
Practise planning trades at memestreet.net.

